Claim 1 claims a co-erectile magnetic resonance integrated coil for penile, corpora cavernosa imaging, comparative document 1 (CN104822318A, publication date: August 5, 2015) is the closest prior art, which (see paragraphs 7-38 of the specification, Figures 1-2) discloses a coil arrangement for a magnetic resonance tomography apparatus (i.e.
Discloses a magnetic resonance integral coil for penis), a closed coil, enclosing the scrotum and penis, a third coil sits in the form of a V-shape at the right and left bands with a lower longitudinal side, such that the scrotum and penis pass through the opening of the coil, the coils are housed in a flexible cushion that largely conforms to the form of the individual body of the patient, the channels for the penis and scrotum must be present in the cushion (equivalent to the cover including a shield (10) with the second coil (7) embedded in the body), and Figure 1 discloses having a securing
strap arrangement (i.e. A securing strap is disclosed).
The solution claimed in claim 1 is compared to the solution disclosed in Comparative Document 1, its distinguishing technical features are: (1) a sleeve (1) connected to a shroud (10), the connection between the sleeve (1) and the shroud (10) is a flexible connection, the sleeve (1) and shield (10) are each of resin material, the sleeve (1) is embedded in the body with a first coil (6), the first coil (6) and second coil (7) are each a multi-channel magnetic resonance imaging coil that is plugged through an adaptor to a coil interface of a magnetic resonance imaging device; (2) the magnetic resonance all-in-one coil is further used for assisting cavernosal imaging of bob, the all-in-one coil further comprising a negative pressure attractive bob device and a programmable erection level control system; the negative-pressure attractive bobbin device comprises a negative-pressure cylinder (2) disposed within the cavity of the sleeve (1) and a negative-pressure aspirator (5) connected between the negative-pressure cylinder (2) and the negative-pressure aspirator
(5), the negative-pressure tube (3) being provided with a pressure gauge (4); the negative pressure cartridge (2) is provided with an exhaust hole (9) at which a first butterfly needle valve is provided; the programmable erection level control system comprising a controller (12) to which both the negative pressure aspirator (5) and the pressure gauge (4) are connected, the controller (12) being configured to control the magnitude of pressure, the rate of pressure change and the duration of pressure duration within the negative pressure tube (2); the front end of the negative pressure cartridge (2) is provided with a contrast agent injection hole (8) at which a second butterfly needle valve is provided and connected by a line to a fully automated magnetic resonance contrast agent injection system. Based on the distinguishing technical features, the technical problem actually solved by the present claims is (1) an alternative coil
